    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="HHDBDA5CA67301EFDD66D710464B3B3AAB" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
Incorporated May 13, 1852 pursuant to an Act of the Massachusetts Legislature which is Chapter 208 of the Acts of 1852. Pursuant to the provisions of Chapter 385 of the Acts of 1887, by and order dated November 26, 1889, it was authorized to engage in the business of generating and furnishing electricity.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;The name of the Company was changed to Fitchburg Gas and Electric Light Company December 5, 1895.</div>
    </link:footnote>
